[{'id': 40666, 'title': None, 'body': '<p>If I get this right you want a vector that is normal to the screen plane but in world coordinates?</p> <p>In that case you want to <code>INVERT</code> the transformation from <code>World -&gt; Screen and do Screen -&gt; World</code> of <code>(00-1)</code> or <code>(001)</code> depending on which axis the screen points down.</p> <p>Since the ModelView matrix is just a rotation matrix (ignoring the homogeneous transformation part) you can simply pull this out by taking the transpose of the rotational part or simple reading in the bottom row - as this transposes onto the <code>Z</code> coordinate column under transposition.</p>', 'accepted_answer_id': None, 'answer_count': None, 'comment_count': 0, 'community_owned_date': 'NaT', 'creation_date': '2008-09-02 21:05:56.027000+00:00', 'favorite_count': None, 'last_activity_date': '2016-02-20 16:39:00.497000+00:00', 'last_edit_date': '2016-02-20 16:39:00.497000+00:00', 'last_editor_display_name': None, 'last_editor_user_id': 2004685, 'owner_display_name': 'caramelcarrot', 'owner_user_id': 3877, 'parent_id': 40028, 'post_type_id': 2, 'score': 2, 'tags': '', 'view_count': None}, {'id': 14591272, 'title': None, 'body': '<p>Operator precedence. The ternary operator has the third lowest precedence in C so the addition is evaluated before it could get to the conditional part. Use parentheses:</p> <pre><code>return ([[self obj1] integerValue] == -1 ? 0 : [[self obj1] integerValue]) + ([[self obj2] integerValue] == -1 ? 0 : [[self obj2] integerValue]) + ([[self obj3] integerValue] == -1 ? 0 : [[self obj3] integerValue]); </code></pre>', 'accepted_answer_id': None, 'answer_count': None, 'comment_count': 0, 'community_owned_date': 'NaT', 'creation_date': '2013-01-29 20:06:33.473000+00:00', 'favorite_count': None, 'last_activity_date': '2013-07-08 21:18:33.230000+00:00', 'last_edit_date': '2013-07-08 21:18:33.230000+00:00', 'last_editor_display_name': 'user529758', 'last_editor_user_id': None, 'owner_display_name': 'user529758', 'owner_user_id': None, 'parent_id': 14591209, 'post_type_id': 2, 'score': 4, 'tags': '', 'view_count': None}, {'id': 168696, 'title': None, 'body': '<p>Customize the variable c-default-style. You either want your Other mode (or php if its available) set to bsd or you can set hte style in all modes to bsd.</p> <p>From what I understand PHP mode is built on top of c mode so it inherits its customizations.</p>', 'accepted_answer_id': None, 'answer_count': None, 'comment_count': 0, 'community_owned_date': 'NaT', 'creation_date': '2008-10-03 20:17:51.193000+00:00', 'favorite_count': None, 'last_activity_date': '2008-10-03 20:17:51.193000+00:00', 'last_edit_date': 'NaT', 'last_editor_display_name': None, 'last_editor_user_id': None, 'owner_display_name': 'Jonathan Arkell', 'owner_user_id': 11052, 'parent_id': 168621, 'post_type_id': 2, 'score': 1, 'tags': '', 'view_count': None}, {'id': 484865, 'title': None, 'body': '<p>Install <a href= http://www.microsoft.com/downloadS/details.aspx?FamilyID=28bd5941-c458-46f1-b24d-f60151d875a3&amp;displaylang=en rel= nofollow >Debug Diag</a> and monitor your app he generate DUMP file for you and have analyze to.<br></p>', 'accepted_answer_id': None, 'answer_count': None, 'comment_count': 0, 'community_owned_date': 'NaT', 'creation_date': '2009-01-27 19:29:52.240000+00:00', 'favorite_count': None, 'last_activity_date': '2009-02-26 14:09:24.957000+00:00', 'last_edit_date': '2009-02-26 14:09:24.957000+00:00', 'last_editor_display_name': 'lsalamon', 'last_editor_user_id': 47733, 'owner_display_name': 'lsalamon', 'owner_user_id': 47733, 'parent_id': 484727, 'post_type_id': 2, 'score': 1, 'tags': '', 'view_count': None}, {'id': 653886, 'title': None, 'body': "<p>On windows 2003 the first thing I look at when there is a problem like that is to look at the browser permissions relating to the site. It could be that your IE settings won't allow it to use the silverlight control. </p>", 'accepted_answer_id': None, 'answer_count': None, 'comment_count': 0, 'community_owned_date': 'NaT', 'creation_date': '2009-03-17 11:45:53.237000+00:00', 'favorite_count': None, 'last_activity_date': '2009-03-17 11:45:53.237000+00:00', 'last_edit_date': 'NaT', 'last_editor_display_name': None, 'last_editor_user_id': None, 'owner_display_name': 'Kevin', 'owner_user_id': 1942, 'parent_id': 653874, 'post_type_id': 2, 'score': 0, 'tags': '', 'view_count': None}]

