[{'id': 32669925, 'text': "What is there to say?  In array context, as provided by `my @fileData`, the `<>` operator reads lines into the array with an implicit loop.  It works.  Occasionally, it is useful. Perl has a couple of mottos.  One is TMTOWTDI — There's More Than One Way To Do It.  Another is DWIM — Do What I Mean; at least, Perl does this more than many languages, provided you know what you're asking for.  This is a piece of dwimmery.", 'creation_date': '2014-02-07 06:35:37.693000+00:00', 'post_id': 21620857, 'user_id': 15168, 'user_display_name': None, 'score': 5}, {'id': 32670020, 'text': '... and it takes 2 seconds to add it to windows (8.1 in my case) > Control Panel > Add Programes > Turn windows features on', 'creation_date': '2014-02-07 06:39:30.367000+00:00', 'post_id': 8920568, 'user_id': 81053, 'user_display_name': None, 'score': 30}, {'id': 32670048, 'text': 'Yes, the 4th argument being "0" causes the replaecment string to be inserted without overwriting any of the original string.', 'creation_date': '2014-02-07 06:40:59.910000+00:00', 'post_id': 17880260, 'user_id': 631764, 'user_display_name': None, 'score': 14}, {'id': 32670086, 'text': 'See here https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Member_Operators', 'creation_date': '2014-02-07 06:42:53.817000+00:00', 'post_id': 21620988, 'user_id': 670396, 'user_display_name': None, 'score': 5}, {'id': 32670116, 'text': "The question didn't ask for encryption and decryption. It only asked for key pair generation. And encryption and decryption is very well explained in documentation.", 'creation_date': '2014-02-07 06:44:10.983000+00:00', 'post_id': 20877180, 'user_id': 1468663, 'user_display_name': None, 'score': 24}]

